// B1 course (A2 → B1 roadmap), module 12 „Ilm, loodus ja keskkond” (a2b1-056…060), stage B1. Final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md; how: docs/FINAL_SHAPE_AUTHORING.md). One storyline in June and early July, after the
// shopping module: a hot week in Tallinn, jaanipäev at Viktor's farm in Kõrvemaa (the family comes in the used Škoda,
// Sofia and Helgi by train to Aegviidu), a thunderstorm on the bog boardwalk (Muki runs away), the storm of the night
// after jaanipäev (a birch on the sauna roof, 30 hours without electricity, the insurance), and the shared courtyard of
// Valgevase 7 and 3 in Kalamaja after the storm. The goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner agrees with the
// neighbours on one green project for the courtyard (Harno S1b) and does the first full, timed mock exam.
//   056 KUUL L→W  „Palav nädal ja jaanipäeva ilm” — five radio forecasts (numbers by ear), läheb jahedamaks / muutub
//                 tuuliseks, the weather service page (true / false / not stated), dictation of warnings, an information
//                 gap on two days' weather, Eksaminurk L2 (radio „Päevateema” with meteorologist Ragnar Vaher); Kasuta:
//                 Viktor's voicemail → notes, the call to the village hall (Ants), a voice message to Jaan, the letter to
//                 Lena about jaanipäev and the weather (main).
//   057 LUGU R→W  „Äike rabas” — the story episode (predict, then read; cliffhanger: Muki is gone), Oskar tells Rasmus
//                 about jaanilaupäev (who did what), kui / enne kui / pärast seda, kui and the narrative past, retold
//                 twice; RMK-style notices on the radio, a hiker's checklist with a word bank, Eksaminurk R2 (an article on
//                 thunderstorms in nature); Kasuta: Oskar's diary, where to look for Muki (ranking), Mia's version
//                 recorded at home, the end of the story (main, W05).
//   058 AVAS R→S  „Torm talus: miks ja mis siis?” — try first, then the local news; B1 grammar spiral: cause and result
//                 (sest, kuna, … tõttu / pärast, seepärast / seetõttu + verb, nii et), rule, try again, 4-3-2, relaying
//                 to Sofia; Jaan's call to Viktor, notices after the storm, Eksaminurk R3a (the parish paper), joining
//                 sentences, word formation (tormine, kuumus), the neighbour's spruce on the fence; Kasuta: the same
//                 situation again — the insurance terms and Viktor's list, the call to the insurer (main), a voice
//                 message to Helgi, a written answer to the insurer.
//   059 RÄÄK L→S  „Roheline hoov: lepime kokku” — a radio interview on waste (true / false), opinion + reason +
//                 example, verb government (hoolima millest, loobuma millest, osalema millel), the house chat, a survey
//                 of three people, Tiina's draft made polite; services for old things (R1), neighbours' voicemails,
//                 crossword, the association's sorting rules, Joosep's draft, topic questions twice; Kasuta: three
//                 proposals, Eksaminurk S1b = the agreement at the meeting (main), a summary recorded at home, the
//                 invitation to the clean-up day.
//   060 PROOV     Mock 1 (§6.1, §6.5): the first full, timed Harno B1 mock — R1, R2, R3b, R4 (33 p, 50 min) · L1, L2,
//                 L3b, L4 (30 p) · W1a, W2b (20 p) · S0, S1a, S1b, S2 (20 p); checkpoint 60 % per part (R 20, L 18,
//                 W 12, S 12) → a catch-up plan for modules 13–15 below it; target 80 %; warm-up sheet with the end of
//                 the summer story.
// B1 grammar (METHODOLOGY_STANDARD §7, grammarPlan.js): module 12 adds no new item; it spirals cause and result (058 AVAS,
// grammarPlan 'cause'), the translative of change in weather (läheb jahedamaks, muutub tuuliseks: 056, module 7), the
// narrative past and the pluperfect with kui / enne kui (057, modules 5 and 10), verb government (059, module 8) and the
// impersonal of forecasts and notices (oodatakse, soovitatakse, pannakse). §6.2 row 12 is used as written: KUUL L→W ·
// LUGU R→W · AVAS R→S · RÄÄK L→S · Mock 1. Cast (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): new — meteorologist Ragnar Vaher (radio, host
// Ülle), village hall head Ants, Viktor's neighbour Ülo, Rasmus (Oskar's friend), insurer „Kodukaitse” (Egle), waste
// adviser Mailis Raudsepp (radio). Earlier versions: archive/v3/b1/module12.js, archive/v1/b1/module12.js.
